    authority: Kelly Trout, Greg Muttitt, Dimitri Lafleur, Thijs Van de Graaf, 
      Roman Mendelevitch, Lan Mei, Malte Meinshausen
    url: https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/ac6228
    description: 'Environ. Res. Lett. 17, 064010 (published version via Ghent University
      repository; IOP blocks scripts). Abstract and Sect. 3.2 (p. 5): developed reserves
      (existing and under-construction fields and mines) commit 936 GtCO2 (90 % CI
      880-992): coal 47 % (446), oil 35 % (323), gas 18 %. Staying within a 1.5 °C
      budget (50 %) means leaving almost 40 % of developed reserves unextracted.;
      Attachment: source_material/science/fossil-supply/Trout-et-al-2022-existing-fossil-extraction-beyond-1p5C-ERL.pdf;
      Format: Journal article; Licensing: CC BY 4.0; Geographic Coverage: Global;
      Date Last Updated: 2022-05-17; Updated by: Environmental Research Letters (IOP)'
